  "source": "Ours (GROUND.md §6.6). The Tin Finch TF-01's sizes, sockets, skids and nozzles come from its asset (D:/GameDev/Assets/TinFinch_TF01: socket_manifest.json and the source geometry, in the game model's axes: +Z the nose, +Y up, +X the left side, metres from the pivot on the ground between the skids). Mass, thrust, rates and drag are chosen for a weighty, thrust-borne skiff flown the Elite way (flight assist on by default, boost); drag areas are Cd x area. The hull's 750 is Rust's minicopter's; it burns lamp oil, our low-grade fuel, as Rust's helicopters burn theirs. The air comes from the planet (the zone's spec), not from here. P2 (GROUND_SYSTEMS.md §6): placed from its item (placement.json's ship rule with its own 'placement' on top), its hull must be clear and its skids on the ground or a foundation's top no steeper than 20 degrees (the vehicle workbench bay's slope), within 12 m of the eye; it carries fuel.placed of lamp oil, the same 50 its recipe's first tank holds.",
